- `canMerge16` should use `<` and `>=` to check for overlap OR adjacency

But both functions have the same logical structure. Let me verify if the issue is really in `canMerge16` by creating a simple test program based on the PR description.

```bash
cat <<'EOF' > test_merge.go
package main

import (
	"fmt"
)

// Assuming interval16 has start and last methods that return uint16
type interval16 struct {
	start uint16
	last  uint16
}

func (i interval16) startValue() uint16 {
	return i.start
}

func (i interval16) lastValue() uint16 {
	return i.last
}

func canMerge16(a, b interval16) bool {
	if int(a.last())+1 < int(b.start) {
		return false
	}
	return int(b.last())+1 >= int(a.start)
}

